      "writtenOn": "2025-02-17T08:58:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you have a reference for the decision to keep the STM open all the time on D3D11 for Graphit? Do we have a conclusive resolution that it is the only way to minimize submits? It might happen to work on this exact configuration but in all the other backends it would cause a bunch of issues. When/if we switch to D3D11 Deferred contexts for multi threading it will also stop working etc.\n\nAlso exposing a \"public\", backend-agnostic API to set the initialized state of any texture makes it seem like this will always be supported and safe to call, when it isn\u0027t (some backends have it semi-tied to the barrier state).",
      "revId": "f263ec69dbf4414a971071a6efa3aeff5106f9c9",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f8822f9d_fd023e66",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-17T09:06:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is only meant for `SharedTextureMemoryD3D11Texture2D` where the ID3D11Texture2D is imported into Dawn unlike `SharedTextureMemoryDXGISharedHandle`.\nThat  ID3D11Texture2D is only used by single D3D device. It makes no sense to use fences. Note: even if you deferred contexts, fences are also useless. Fences cannot be used by deferred contexts anw. Deferred contexts has to be inserted to the main context\u0027s stream. Hence Begin/EndAccess makes no sense for `SharedTextureMemoryD3D11Texture2D` and it makes it unnecessariyl complicated to book keeping the accesses.\n\nWe are planning to make small optimization for `SharedTextureMemoryD3D11Texture2D` in chrome. fine-grained Begin/EndAccess is still used for `SharedTextureMemoryDXGISharedHandle`",
      "parentUuid": "264834b4_44312220",
      "revId": "f263ec69dbf4414a971071a6efa3aeff5106f9c9",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c16deca0_480814e8",
